{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>As he passed Penuel.</b> Perhaps it is that the name of the place is not called Penuel but by Jacob alone, whereas everyone besides him — even the verse of Torah itself — calls it Penuel, and so indeed it is called in Judges (8:8)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The import is that Jacob named the place Peniel (with a yod), while the Torah's own narration and all others call it Penuel (with a vav); the Or HaChaim accounts for the discrepancy by noting that Jacob alone used the form Peniel."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:40.205515333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}